SOUND TOOLS AND BUILD PIPELINE
==============================

v1.3.1 notes
------------
- Sound tools are unchanged at the data-format level — the audio
  pipeline (samples → vrom → fm → mml → ssg → m1rom) is the same as
  v1.3.0.  Only the IDs and the demo's USE of the tracks have changed.
- See sound/mml/readme, sound/ssg/readme, and sound/samples/readme
  for the per-stage entry points.

Python 3 tools that process audio assets and prepare them for the Neo Geo.

TOOLS
-----
vrom.py
    Packs ADPCM-A and ADPCM-B samples into the V ROM (<GAME_ID>-v1.v1).
    Auto-generates sound/driver/sample_table.inc with correct start/end offsets.
    Reads GAME_ID from environment (set by Makefile via GAME=<name>).

mml_compile.py
    Compiles MML source files (games/<GAME>/sound/mml/*.mml) into Z80 data
    tables (sound/driver/music_data.inc) for the SSG/MML music engine.

fm_compile.py
    Compiles FM MML source files (games/<GAME>/sound/fm/*.mml) into Z80 data
    tables (sound/driver/fm_data.inc) for the FM sequencer. Includes 128-entry
    note frequency table (BLOCK/FNUM pairs) and compiled track byte streams.

fm_patch_compile.py
    Compiles the FM patch bank (games/<GAME>/sound/fm/patches.fm) into a Z80
    data table (sound/driver/fm_patch_table.inc). Supports up to 16 named
    patches with full operator parameters (DT/MUL, TL, AR, DR, SR, SL/RR, ENV)
    plus algorithm, feedback, stereo, and LFO fields.

ssg_compile.py
    Compiles standalone SSG MML source files (games/<GAME>/sound/ssg/*.mml)
    into Z80 data tables (sound/driver/ssg_data.inc) for the standalone SSG
    sequencer.

ssg_config_compile.py
    Compiles the SSG tone preset config (games/<GAME>/sound/ssg/config.ssg)
    into a Z80 data table (sound/driver/ssg_config.inc) for soundSetSSGPreset().

adpcm_enc.py
    Python encoder: converts WAV files to Neo Geo ADPCM-A or ADPCM-B format.

enc_wave16le_a.sh / enc_wave16le_b.sh
    Batch-convert source WAVs to raw 16-bit mono PCM at the target sample rate
    used by the ADPCM encoders. Use the bundled Python converter by default.
    SoX is used only when SOX is explicitly set.

wav_to_raw_pcm.py
    Dependency-free WAV converter used by default on both Linux and Windows.
    Produces raw signed little-endian 16-bit PCM.

adpcm_enc_process.sh
    Processes all raw WAV inputs in samples/in_wav_* through the encoder.

m1rom.sh / m1rom.bat
    Assembles driver.asm with wla-z80, links with wlalink, pads output to
    128 KB and copies result to out/<GAME_ID>-m1.m1 and roms/neogeosdk/.
    Reads GAME_ID and GAME_SOUND from environment (set by Makefile).
    Expects all .inc files to be pre-generated (run via make m1rom which
    invokes fmpatches, fm, mml, ssgconfig, ssg targets first).

vrom.sh / vrom.bat
    Runs vrom.py and copies the result to roms/neogeosdk/<GAME_ID>-v1.v1.
    Reads GAME_ID from environment.

BUILD COMMANDS
--------------
  make sound      : samples + vrom + fmpatches + fm + mml + ssgconfig + ssg + m1rom
  make sound-all  : alias for make sound
  make vrom       : V ROM only (pack samples, update table)
  make mml        : compile SSG/MML music data (sound/mml → music_data.inc)
  make fm         : compile FM MML data (sound/fm → fm_data.inc)
  make fmpatches  : compile FM patch bank (sound/fm/patches.fm → fm_patch_table.inc)
  make ssg        : compile standalone SSG data (sound/ssg → ssg_data.inc)
  make ssgconfig  : compile SSG config (sound/ssg/config.ssg → ssg_config.inc)
  make m1rom      : assemble Z80 driver (auto-runs fmpatches fm mml ssgconfig ssg)
  make samples    : re-encode raw WAVs to ADPCM

Native Windows equivalents:

  make -f MakefileWin32.mak sound
  make -f MakefileWin32.mak samples
  make -f MakefileWin32.mak m1rom
  make -f MakefileWin32.mak m1rom-c

Environment overrides:

  Linux:
    make samples
    PYTHON=python3.12 SOX=/usr/local/bin/sox make samples

  Windows:
    make -f MakefileWin32.mak samples
    make -f MakefileWin32.mak samples PY=py SOX=C:\path\to\sox.exe

REQUIREMENTS
------------
  Python 3.x, numpy, wla-dx (wla-z80 and wlalink), srecord
  SoX is optional and disabled by default; set SOX explicitly to use it.
